                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df772ce8-fd14-48d1-a7aa-311d899258f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe02ceec-ffae-3665-8f54-c580b67c34e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "42e43737-4e59-3693-b430-a97085c6d21d",
                        "target_lang_word": "disgrace",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being out of favor; loss of favor, regard, or respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc174b0-9d1e-4575-ac38-d9b3727b12c9",
                                                "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                                "text": "I heare / Macduffe liues in diſgrace. Sir, can you tell / Where he beſtowes himſelfe?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being dishonored, or covered with shame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7756053a-8f4a-47b8-a6dc-35ce986c9d1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                                "text": "Now she lives in disgrace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which brings dishonor; the cause of reproach or shame; great discredit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6366a8e0-9952-49d6-826e-46e7372d03ac",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "His behaviour at the party was a total disgrace! He was leeching on all the ladies, and insulting the men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0e8ca50-9b33-4a8d-8471-0825a5e950d1",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "Practice and whipping were alike unavailing, and Epps, satisfied of it at last, swore I was a disgrace—that I was not fit to associate with a cotton-picking \"nigger\"—that I could not pick enough in a day to pay the trouble of weighing it, and that I should go into the cotton field no more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of unkindness; a disfavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "358e13b3-720c-4406-b42c-04b97bbfb423",
                                                "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                                "text": "As for the pulling of them [ambitious men] downe, if the Affaires require it, and that it may not be done with ſafety ſuddainly, the onely Way is, the Enterchange, continually of Fauours, and Diſgraces, whereby they may not know, what to expect; And be, as it were, in a Wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                        "entry_id": "3de008e8-961c-3a15-a0c5-566717b3bb8c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put someone or something out of favor; to bring shame or ignominy upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07fe5c7-a9db-4a30-a640-26c42383455e",
                                                "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                                "text": "[…] some families renounced the use of a certain praenomen which had been disgraced by one of their name […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2f1e452-c955-4d10-85be-20e5a83aabd7",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe02ceec-ffae-3665-8f54-c580b67c34e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "42e43737-4e59-3693-b430-a97085c6d21d",
                        "target_lang_word": "défaveur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "défaveur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                        "entry_id": "2cc36fd4-a0da-307c-9c22-ee16af1fc902",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cessation de faveur, disgrâce."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a831ba61-b3d4-42fe-99c5-8674ab2336e3",
                                                "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                                "text": "Il est tombé dans une cruelle défaveur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9a2937d-f955-467f-bfb0-ed52eb665acc",
                                                "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                                "text": "Il est en défaveur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05d9ed40-e509-40ce-b140-5acf3812e4e2",
                                                "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                                "text": "Plus des deux tiers ne dépassèrent pas cinquante dollars, témoignant avec une vigueur manifeste de la défaveur dans laquelle ce genre de peinture était tombé depuis le début du siècle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6fe05b4-3301-480c-90aa-c2480d0c9143",
                                                "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                                "text": "Or il se produit quelque chose qui se produit généralement dans toutes les armées du monde, c’est le piston, pas en ma faveur, mais en ma défaveur, et cette défaveur va me faire rester en Algérie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d1c5dd4-7bd0-4b94-95fe-fb35ccfc73cc",
                                                "sense_id": "728078b8-0a28-316f-a1cf-8f8bd9a0d990",
                                                "text": "La balance du pouvoir au sein du Parti conservateur du Canada (PCC) penchera dorénavant en défaveur des provinces comme le Québec, quand viendra le temps de choisir le prochain chef."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08183070-47bf-4f15-8f81-eaaa863eb25d",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe02ceec-ffae-3665-8f54-c580b67c34e1",
                        "source_sense_id": "42e43737-4e59-3693-b430-a97085c6d21d",
                        "target_lang_word": "discrédit",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "discrédit",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe2de52f-45fc-382c-b4d8-e5f352ff4f97",
                                        "entry_id": "70a840ea-a8a1-3302-8c8a-f9ac0074b877",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Diminution du crédit dont jouissait une personne ou une chose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff97f1ca-5387-4288-be14-eec72b273e01",
                                                "sense_id": "fe2de52f-45fc-382c-b4d8-e5f352ff4f97",
                                                "text": "Le jeune homme avait affirmé qu'il s’en fichait. L'essentiel n'était-il pas le résultat ? La réputation, le crédit, le discrédit, tout ça, il s'en branlait, avait-il finement précisé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85413724-5429-4aaa-acee-5d2f25f84bde",
                                                "sense_id": "fe2de52f-45fc-382c-b4d8-e5f352ff4f97",
                                                "text": "Coût politique enfin, avec le discrédit qui frappe les dirigeants des pays avancés et, par-delà les personnes, l’extrême dévalorisation que subit la parole publique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd53bac6-affd-4c5c-96ca-e94584b928ed",
                                                "sense_id": "fe2de52f-45fc-382c-b4d8-e5f352ff4f97",
                                                "text": "Pendant ce temps, l’accusation des communautaristes les plus exacerbés qui s’affichent au côté des Frères musulmans, s’abat sur les défenseurs de la laïcité, traînés dans la boue de l’insulte en « laïcardise » ou en « islamophobie », fonction de l’ampleur du discrédit que leurs contempteurs entendent leur infliger."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
